      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Papilloma is a rare primary heart tumour; only 75 cases have been reported and most were casual findings at autopsy. We describe another case of this tumour in a 9 years girl. The neoformation had produced a picture of angina pectoris, followed by death due to an occluded left coronary orifice. To our knowledge, this is the first report of this type of tumour with electrocardiographic documentation."},
